{"event_id": "efd66c608136", "event_type": "system_response", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T19:26:20.305453+00:00", "data": {"text": "We're running the trusty nginx/1.24.0 web server on this Ubuntu 22.04.3 LTS server. It's listening on port 80, and the configuration is a simple Nginx server block that looks like this:\n\n```\nserver {\n    listen 80;\n    server_name example.com;\n\n    location / {\n        index index.html index.htm index.nginx-debian.html;\n        root /var/www/html;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThat's the default configuration, but we've added a few extra rules to make things more interesting. The server is running on a kernel 5.15.0-91, and I'm keeping an eye on it with the usual sysadmin tools, like `journalctl` and `systemctl`. Would you like to know more about our setup?", "persona_used": "novice"}, "source": "harness"}
